cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the instance family, please cite the manuscript below."
title: "Exact test problems and a work-accuracy protocol for benchmarking nearest correlation matrix solvers"
authors:
  - family-names: Ibrahim
    given-names: Oyeyinka E.
    affiliation: "Department of Industrial and Systems Engineering, Northern Illinois University"
abstract: >-
  An NCM instance family with closed-form primal and dual solutions and independently
  controlled rank, near-zero multiplicity and eigenvalue separation, together with a
  matched-accuracy measurement protocol, used to show that the conclusions of nearest
  correlation matrix solver comparisons depend on the stopping rule, the accuracy target,
  the problem dimension, the solution rank and the degree of invalidity, on synthetic,
  literature and equity-derived matrices.
keywords:
  - nearest correlation matrix
  - semidefinite programming
  - benchmarking
  - reproducibility
  - semismooth Newton
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Realosunboy6/ncm-exact-benchmark"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-12"
